---
// firma2-rich-text — a block of formatted text you write in place: paragraphs,
// two heading levels, bulleted and numbered lists, quotes, bold, italic, links.
// What you see while typing is what everyone reads; there is no edit mode.
//
// THE FORMATTING COMES TO THE SELECTION. At rest the text carries no chrome — a
// page is read far more often than it is written, and a toolbar over every read
// is noise. Select some text and a toolbar appears above it (the Medium /
// Notion bubble). Typing carries the rest without a mouse: "## " starts a
// heading, "### " a subheading, "- " a list, "1. " a numbered list, "> " a
// quote, and Mod+B / Mod+I / Mod+K work as everywhere else.
//
// AN EMPTY LINE OFFERS WHAT CAN START THERE: heading, list, image, file — a
// small toolbar beside the caret on a blank line (the Medium "+"). Images and
// files also arrive by pasting or dropping them into the text. Select an image
// and its toolbar is Alt text and Remove instead of the formatting; a
// file, Remove.
//
// AS A CANVAS (the `canvas` prop) it takes the grammar every builder shares —
// docs/adr/0001-one-editing-grammar-for-builder-canvases.md, the same as the
// intake form builder: type `/` for the list of what can go here
// (bcn-insert-menu); hover a block for its grip, which drags it and opens
// Duplicate, Move up, Move down, Turn into and Delete; ⌘D duplicates the block
// the caret is in and ⌥↑ ⌥↓ move it. Off by default: an editor inside another
// canvas (the intake builder's text blocks) leaves grips and `/` to its host.
//
// A FILE SITS IN THE TEXT WHERE IT WAS PUT, as an image does. A PDF shows a
// PREVIEW right there — the browser's own PDF reader, held to a part of the
// window so the text around it still reads as text — with its name and a
// download under it (esa-file-list), and beside them Full screen and Open in
// new tab for reading the whole thing. Any other format is the
// name-and-download row alone; so is a PDF in a browser set to download PDFs.
//
// CONTRACT:
//   in   `firma2:rich-text-mount` dispatched on a root added after load
//        (bubbling) — mounts it. Roots present at load mount themselves.
//        The component must also be rendered once outside a <template>,
//        or its script never runs.
//   in   `firma2:rich-text-set` on the root, {html} — replaces the content
//        without counting as an edit
//   in   `firma2:rich-text-editable` on the root, {editable} — view or edit.
//        Read-only, the text is plain reading: no caret, no toolbars, no
//        placeholder, and a link opens on a plain click.
//   prop `canvas` — the builder grammar above (custom pages)
//   in   `firma2:rich-text-focus` on the root — puts the caret at the end
//        (the rail's Edit page)
//   out  `firma2:rich-text-change` from the root, {html} — after typing settles
//        (300ms), bubbling
//   out  `firma2:rich-text-error` from the root, {message} — a file it refused
//   hook `root.firma2StoreImage(file) → {src, fileId}` — where an image goes.
//        Set by the page; without it an image lives only as long as the tab.
//        `fileId` is written to the <img> as data-file-id, which is what lets
//        the page find the image again after a reload.
//   hook `root.firma2StoreFile(file) → {src, fileId}` — the same, for a file.
//   hook `root.firma2FileUrl(fileId) → Promise<url | undefined>` — where a
//        stored file is read from now. A file is saved as an empty
//        <div data-file-embed data-file-id data-name data-type data-size>;
//        its URL is never saved, because it dies with the tab.
// The HTML goes through the editor's schema on the way in, so anything it does
// not know — scripts, styles, unknown tags, javascript: links — is dropped
// before it reaches the page. That is what makes stored HTML safe to render.
//
// bcn-lego-checked: no esa- rich text or contenteditable lego exists (walked
// `ls node_modules/@esa/ecology/src/components/`: esa-textarea is plain text,
// esa-popover anchors to a trigger element, not to a text selection). Beacon is
// not cloned on this machine. The editor is Tiptap (ProseMirror); every button
// is esa-button, the link field is esa-text-field in esa-dialog, and the layout
// is `.cluster`. What is bespoke: the toolbar's floating surface — esa-popover's
// own surface tokens (raised background, default border, radius-md,
// elevation-4) on an element Tiptap positions — and the typeset of the content,
// which is typography composites on every block plus list and quote spacing.
// A file in the text is esa-file-list (its row) and esa-button (Full screen,
// Open in new tab, cloned from a template); the PDF preview frame is the one
// element drawn here, framed as firma2-document-viewer frames its own — no
// esa- lego shows a document.
// firma2-rich-text is the reusable home: any long-form field that needs
// structure renders it. As a canvas: the `/` list is bcn-insert-menu and the
// grip is esa-dropdown-menu around a chrome esa-button. The grip drags with
// ProseMirror's own block drag, not @tiptap/extension-drag-handle, whose v3
// requires the Yjs collaboration packages as peers.
import EsaButton from '@esa/ecology/esa-button.astro';

interface Props {
  /** Accessible name of the text area — "Page content". */
  label: string;
  /** Shown in an empty editor. */
  placeholder?: string;
  /** The builder grammar: `/`, block grips, ⌘D and ⌥↑ ⌥↓. For a page you write. */
  canvas?: boolean;
}

const { label, placeholder = '', canvas = false } = Astro.props;

// Order: inline marks, then block types, then the link. Labels are the names a
// screen reader announces and the tooltip shows.
const IMAGE_MAX_MB = 10;
// The same cap as Add document.
const FILE_MAX_MB = 25;
const tools = [
  { cmd: 'bold', icon: 'bold', label: 'Bold' },
  { cmd: 'italic', icon: 'italic', label: 'Italic' },
  { cmd: 'heading-2', icon: 'heading-2', label: 'Heading' },
  { cmd: 'heading-3', icon: 'heading-3', label: 'Subheading' },
  { cmd: 'bullet-list', icon: 'list', label: 'Bulleted list' },
  { cmd: 'ordered-list', icon: 'list-ordered', label: 'Numbered list' },
  { cmd: 'blockquote', icon: 'text-quote', label: 'Quote' },
  { cmd: 'link', icon: 'link', label: 'Link' },
];
// What a blank line can become. Image opens the file picker.
const inserts = [
  { cmd: 'heading-2', icon: 'heading-2', label: 'Heading' },
  { cmd: 'bullet-list', icon: 'list', label: 'Bulleted list' },
  { cmd: 'ordered-list', icon: 'list-ordered', label: 'Numbered list' },
  { cmd: 'image', icon: 'image', label: 'Image' },
  { cmd: 'file', icon: 'paperclip', label: 'File' },
];
---
<div class="firma2-rich-text" data-rich-text data-canvas={canvas ? '' : undefined} data-label={label} data-placeholder={placeholder} data-image-max-mb={IMAGE_MAX_MB} data-file-max-mb={FILE_MAX_MB}>
  <div data-rich-text-editor></div>

  {/* Taken out of the document by Tiptap on mount and put back, positioned,
      whenever there is a selection. Hidden until then so it never flashes. */}
  <div class="firma2-rich-text__toolbar cluster" data-gap="xs" role="toolbar" aria-label="Formatting" data-rich-text-toolbar>
    {tools.map((t) => (
      <EsaButton variant="chrome" size="sm" iconOnly icon={t.icon} label={t.label} data-cmd={t.cmd} data-for="text" aria-pressed="false" />
    ))}
    {/* A selected image swaps the formatting for what an image can take. */}
    <EsaButton variant="chrome" size="md" data-cmd="alt" data-for="image">Alt text</EsaButton>
    <EsaButton variant="chrome" size="md" data-cmd="remove-image" data-for="image">Remove</EsaButton>
    {/* A selected file: the one thing a file can take here. */}
    <EsaButton variant="chrome" size="md" data-cmd="remove-file" data-for="file">Remove</EsaButton>
  </div>

  {/* A PDF preview's two ways to read the whole thing, cloned into each one. */}
  <template data-file-actions>
    <div class="cluster" data-gap="xs">
      <EsaButton variant="chrome" size="sm" iconOnly icon="maximize" label="Full screen" data-file-fullscreen />
      <EsaButton variant="chrome" size="sm" iconOnly icon="external-link" label="Open in new tab" data-file-open />
    </div>
  </template>

  {/* The blank-line toolbar. Same surface, same lifecycle (Tiptap's floating menu). */}
  <div class="firma2-rich-text__toolbar firma2-rich-text__inserts cluster" data-gap="xs" role="toolbar" aria-label="Insert" data-rich-text-inserts>
    {inserts.map((t) => (
      <EsaButton variant="chrome" size="sm" iconOnly icon={t.icon} label={t.label} data-cmd={t.cmd} />
    ))}
  </div>

  {canvas && (
    <>
      <bcn-insert-menu aria-label="Insert" data-rich-text-slash></bcn-insert-menu>
      {/* The grip of the block under the pointer, moved beside it. */}
      <esa-dropdown-menu class="firma2-rich-text__grip" position="below-start" draggable="true" hidden data-rich-text-grip>
        <EsaButton variant="chrome" size="md" iconOnly icon="grip-vertical" label="Drag to move, or click for options" />
      </esa-dropdown-menu>
    </>
  )}

  <esa-dialog class="firma2-rich-text__alt-dialog" heading="Alt text" size="sm" show-close-button>
    <esa-textarea
      label="Describe the image"
      help-text="What someone who can’t see it needs to know. Leave it empty if the image is decoration."
      size="md"
      rows="3"
      data-alt-text
    ></esa-textarea>
    <div class="cluster" data-gap="xs" slot="footer">
      <EsaButton variant="primary" size="md" data-alt-save>Save</EsaButton>
      <EsaButton variant="ghost" size="md" data-alt-cancel>Cancel</EsaButton>
    </div>
  </esa-dialog>

  <esa-dialog class="firma2-rich-text__link-dialog" heading="Link" size="sm" show-close-button>
    <esa-text-field label="Web address" size="md" type="url" inputmode="url" placeholder="https://" data-link-url></esa-text-field>
    <div class="cluster" data-gap="xs" slot="footer">
      <EsaButton variant="primary" size="md" data-link-save>Save</EsaButton>
      <EsaButton variant="ghost" size="md" data-link-remove>Remove</EsaButton>
      <EsaButton variant="ghost" size="md" data-link-cancel>Cancel</EsaButton>
    </div>
  </esa-dialog>
</div>

<script>
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-dialog';
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-text-field';
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-textarea';
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-file-list';
  import '@esa/ecology/esa-dropdown-menu';
  import './bcn-insert-menu';
  import type { BcnInsertMenu, InsertItem } from './bcn-insert-menu';
  import { Editor, Extension, Node, mergeAttributes } from '@tiptap/core';
  import type { Range } from '@tiptap/core';
  import Suggestion from '@tiptap/suggestion';
  import { atLimit, limitOf } from '../../lib/plan-usage';
  import { PLAN_NAME, readPlan } from '../../lib/workspace-plan';
  import { NodeSelection, TextSelection } from '@tiptap/pm/state';
  import type { Node as PMNode } from '@tiptap/pm/model';
  import Image from '@tiptap/extension-image';
  import FloatingMenu from '@tiptap/extension-floating-menu';
  import StarterKit from '@tiptap/starter-kit';
  import Heading from '@tiptap/extension-heading';
  import BubbleMenu from '@tiptap/extension-bubble-menu';
  import { Placeholder } from '@tiptap/extensions';

  type Field = HTMLElement & { value: string; errorText: string };
  type Dialog = HTMLElement & { show(): void; close(): void };
  type StoreImage = (file: File) => Promise<{ src: string; fileId?: string } | undefined>;
  type FileUrl = (fileId: string) => Promise<string | undefined>;
  type Root = HTMLElement & { firma2StoreImage?: StoreImage; firma2StoreFile?: StoreImage; firma2FileUrl?: FileUrl };
  type FileList = HTMLElement & { files: { name: string; href?: string }[] };
  type Menu = HTMLElement & { items: { label: string; action?: string; disabled?: boolean; divider?: boolean; variant?: 'default' | 'danger' }[]; open: boolean };

  // What `/` can put on a line, as a canvas.
  const SLASH: InsertItem[] = [
    { id: 'heading-2', label: 'Heading', group: 'Text' },
    { id: 'heading-3', label: 'Subheading', group: 'Text' },
    { id: 'bullet-list', label: 'Bulleted list', group: 'Text' },
    { id: 'ordered-list', label: 'Numbered list', group: 'Text' },
    { id: 'blockquote', label: 'Quote', group: 'Text' },
    { id: 'image', label: 'Image', group: 'Media' },
    { id: 'file', label: 'File', group: 'Media' },
  ];
  // What a block of text can turn into, from its grip.
  const KINDS: { id: string; label: string }[] = [
    { id: 'paragraph', label: 'text' },
    { id: 'heading-2', label: 'heading' },
    { id: 'heading-3', label: 'subheading' },
    { id: 'bullet-list', label: 'bulleted list' },
    { id: 'ordered-list', label: 'numbered list' },
    { id: 'blockquote', label: 'quote' },
  ];
  const kindOf = (node: PMNode): string | null => {
    if (node.type.name === 'heading') return `heading-${node.attrs.level}`;
    return { paragraph: 'paragraph', bulletList: 'bullet-list', orderedList: 'ordered-list', blockquote: 'blockquote' }[node.type.name] ?? null;
  };

  const isPdf = (name: string, type: string): boolean => type === 'application/pdf' || /\.pdf$/i.test(name);
  // Only an explicit false means no reader (older browsers lack the property).
  const canReadPdf = (): boolean => (navigator as Navigator & { pdfViewerEnabled?: boolean }).pdfViewerEnabled !== false;
  const download = (href: string, name: string): void => {
    const a = document.createElement('a');
    a.href = href;
    a.download = name;
    a.click();
  };

  /**
   * A file placed in the text. Saved as an empty, attribute-only <div>; drawn
   * by a node view as the PDF (when it is one) over an esa-file-list row. The
   * node view asks `resolveUrl` for the file's current URL — the editor
   * remembers the ones it made this session, the page's hook finds the rest.
   */
  const FileEmbed = (
    resolveUrl: (fileId: string) => Promise<string | undefined>,
    onMissing: (name: string) => void,
    actions: () => HTMLElement | null,
  ) =>
    Node.create({
      name: 'fileEmbed',
      group: 'block',
      atom: true,
      selectable: true,
      draggable: true,
      addAttributes() {
        const data = (key: string) => ({
          default: null,
          parseHTML: (el: HTMLElement) => el.getAttribute(`data-${key}`),
          renderHTML: (attrs: Record<string, unknown>) => {
            const value = attrs[key === 'file-id' ? 'fileId' : key];
            return value == null ? {} : { [`data-${key}`]: String(value) };
          },
        });
        return { fileId: data('file-id'), name: data('name'), type: data('type'), size: data('size') };
      },
      parseHTML: () => [{ tag: 'div[data-file-embed]' }],
      renderHTML: ({ HTMLAttributes }) => ['div', mergeAttributes(HTMLAttributes, { 'data-file-embed': '' })],
      addNodeView: () => ({ node }) => {
        const { fileId, name, type } = node.attrs as { fileId: string | null; name: string | null; type: string | null };
        const label = name ?? 'File';
        const dom = document.createElement('div');
        dom.className = 'firma2-rich-text__file stack';
        dom.dataset.gap = 'xs';
        dom.contentEditable = 'false';
        const row = document.createElement('esa-file-list') as FileList;
        // The name row, and — on a PDF preview — Full screen and Open in new tab beside it.
        const bar = document.createElement('div');
        bar.className = 'firma2-rich-text__file-bar cluster';
        bar.dataset.gap = 'xs';
        bar.append(row);
        let href: string | undefined;
        void (fileId ? resolveUrl(fileId) : Promise.resolve(undefined)).then((url) => {
          href = url;
          customElements.whenDefined('esa-file-list').then(() => (row.files = [{ name: label, href: url }]));
          if (!url || !isPdf(label, type ?? '') || !canReadPdf()) return;
          const frame = document.createElement('iframe');
          frame.className = 'firma2-rich-text__file-frame';
          frame.title = label;
          frame.src = url;
          dom.prepend(frame);
          const tools = actions();
          if (!tools) return;
          tools.querySelector('[data-file-fullscreen]')?.addEventListener('click', () => void frame.requestFullscreen?.());
          tools.querySelector('[data-file-open]')?.addEventListener('click', () => window.open(url, '_blank', 'noopener'));
          bar.append(tools);
        });
        // The name opens the file in a new tab — never this one, which would
        // strand the reader on a bare blob: URL — and the row's button downloads it.
        row.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
          const link = event.composedPath().find((el): el is HTMLAnchorElement => el instanceof HTMLAnchorElement);
          if (!link?.href) return;
          event.preventDefault();
          window.open(link.href, '_blank', 'noopener');
        });
        row.addEventListener('download', () => (href ? download(href, label) : onMissing(label)));
        dom.append(bar);
        // The buttons are the file's own: a click on one must not move the
        // editor's selection onto the file.
        return { dom, stopEvent: (event: Event) => (event.target as HTMLElement).closest?.('[data-file-fullscreen], [data-file-open]') != null };
      },
    });

  // The <img> keeps which stored file it is. src is this session's object URL
  // and goes stale on reload; data-file-id is what the page resolves it from.
  const PageImage = Image.extend({
    addAttributes() {
      return {
        ...this.parent?.(),
        fileId: {
          default: null,
          parseHTML: (el: HTMLElement) => el.getAttribute('data-file-id'),
          renderHTML: (attrs: { fileId?: string | null }) => (attrs.fileId ? { 'data-file-id': attrs.fileId } : {}),
        },
      };
    },
  }).configure({ HTMLAttributes: { class: 'firma2-rich-text__image' } });

  // Every block takes a typography composite — the rule for all text in this
  // spoke — rather than a size set in this file.
  const HEADING_CLASS: Record<number, string> = { 2: 'typography-heading-md', 3: 'typography-title-strong' };
  const TypesetHeading = Heading.extend({
    renderHTML({ node, HTMLAttributes }) {
      const level = node.attrs.level as number;
      return [`h${level}`, mergeAttributes(HTMLAttributes, { class: HEADING_CLASS[level] ?? '' }), 0];
    },
  }).configure({ levels: [2, 3] });

  const mountRichText = (root: Root) => {
    if (root.hasAttribute('data-mounted')) return;
    root.setAttribute('data-mounted', '');
    const mount = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-rich-text-editor]')!;
    const toolbar = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-rich-text-toolbar]')!;
    const insertBar = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-rich-text-inserts]')!;
    const altDialog = root.querySelector<Dialog>('.firma2-rich-text__alt-dialog')!;
    const altField = root.querySelector<Field>('[data-alt-text]')!;
    const maxBytes = Number(root.dataset.imageMaxMb ?? 10) * 1_000_000;
    const fileMaxBytes = Number(root.dataset.fileMaxMb ?? 25) * 1_000_000;
    // URLs for files placed this session, so a new file draws at once.
    const placed = new Map<string, string>();
    const dialog = root.querySelector<Dialog>('.firma2-rich-text__link-dialog')!;
    const urlField = root.querySelector<Field>('[data-link-url]')!;

    let silent = false;
    let timer: number | undefined;

    // ---- the canvas grammar (custom pages) ----
    const canvas = root.hasAttribute('data-canvas');
    const slash = root.querySelector<BcnInsertMenu>('[data-rich-text-slash]');
    const grip = root.querySelector<Menu>('[data-rich-text-grip]');
    let slashRange: Range | null = null;
    const SlashCommand = Extension.create({
      name: 'slashCommand',
      addProseMirrorPlugins() {
        return [
          Suggestion({
            editor: this.editor,
            char: '/',
            items: () => [],
            command: () => {},
            render: () => ({
              onStart: (props) => {
                slashRange = props.range;
                slash!.items = SLASH;
                slash!.open(props.clientRect?.() ?? props.editor.view.dom, { owner: props.editor.view.dom as HTMLElement, query: props.query });
              },
              onUpdate: (props) => {
                slashRange = props.range;
                slash!.filter(props.query);
              },
              onKeyDown: ({ event }) => slash!.handleKey(event),
              onExit: () => slash!.close(),
            }),
          }),
        ];
      },
    });
    // The top-level block the caret is in (or the selected image or file).
    const caretBlock = (): number | null => {
      const { selection } = editor.state;
      if (selection instanceof NodeSelection && selection.$from.depth === 0) return selection.from;
      return selection.$from.depth >= 1 ? selection.$from.before(1) : null;
    };
    const CanvasKeys = Extension.create({
      name: 'canvasKeys',
      addKeyboardShortcuts() {
        const on = (action: string) => () => {
          const pos = caretBlock();
          return pos == null ? false : blockAction(action, pos);
        };
        return { 'Mod-d': on('duplicate'), 'Alt-ArrowUp': on('up'), 'Alt-ArrowDown': on('down') };
      },
    });

    const editor = new Editor({
      element: mount,
      extensions: [
        StarterKit.configure({
          heading: false,
          code: false,
          codeBlock: false,
          strike: false,
          underline: false,
          horizontalRule: false,
          paragraph: { HTMLAttributes: { class: 'typography-body-md' } },
          // Links follow handleClick below: a plain click opens one while
          // reading, and puts the caret in its text while writing.
          link: {
            openOnClick: false,
            autolink: true,
            defaultProtocol: 'https',
            HTMLAttributes: { rel: 'noopener noreferrer', target: '_blank' },
          },
        }),
        TypesetHeading,
        PageImage,
        FileEmbed(
          async (fileId) => placed.get(fileId) ?? (await root.firma2FileUrl?.(fileId)),
          (name) => fail(`${name} isn’t in this browser any more.`),
          () => {
            const tpl = root.querySelector<HTMLTemplateElement>('template[data-file-actions]');
            return (tpl?.content.firstElementChild?.cloneNode(true) as HTMLElement | undefined) ?? null;
          },
        ),
        Placeholder.configure({ placeholder: root.dataset.placeholder ?? '' }),
        ...(canvas ? [SlashCommand, CanvasKeys] : []),
        FloatingMenu.configure({
          element: insertBar,
          appendTo: () => document.body,
          // Just under the caret's empty line, on the text's own left edge.
          // Not in the margin: the margin is the sidebar's edge on a normal
          // window (measured: it overlapped the rail), and beside the caret
          // it would cover the placeholder. It covers the next block at most,
          // and only until you type.
          options: { strategy: 'fixed', placement: 'bottom-start', offset: 4, flip: true, shift: true },
          // Only for the editor you are typing in. A page with several
          // editors (the intake builder's text blocks) otherwise kept a blank
          // line's toolbar up on an editor nobody was in.
          shouldShow: ({ editor, view, state }) => {
            const { $from, empty } = state.selection;
            return view.hasFocus() && editor.isEditable && empty && $from.depth === 1 && $from.parent.type.name === 'paragraph' && $from.parent.content.size === 0;
          },
        }),
        BubbleMenu.configure({
          element: toolbar,
          // On <body> and fixed: inside the page, a sticky or transformed
          // ancestor becomes the fixed box's frame and the toolbar lands
          // offset from the selection (measured: pushed off the left edge).
          appendTo: () => document.body,
          options: { strategy: 'fixed', placement: 'top', offset: 8 },
        }),
      ],
      editorProps: {
        attributes: {
          role: 'textbox',
          'aria-multiline': 'true',
          'aria-label': root.dataset.label ?? '',
          class: 'firma2-rich-text__content',
        },
        // An image or file pasted or dropped into the text is placed where it lands.
        handlePaste(_view, event) {
          const list = event.clipboardData?.files;
          if (!list?.length) return false;
          void insertDropped(list);
          return true;
        },
        handleDrop(view, event) {
          const list = (event as DragEvent).dataTransfer?.files;
          if (!list?.length) return false;
          const at = view.posAtCoords({ left: event.clientX, top: event.clientY })?.pos;
          void insertDropped(list, at);
          return true;
        },
        handleClick(_view, _pos, event) {
          // Reading, a link is just a link. Writing, a plain click edits its
          // text and Mod+click follows it.
          const link = (event.target as HTMLElement).closest('a');
          if (link && (!editor.isEditable || event.metaKey || event.ctrlKey)) {
            window.open(link.href, '_blank', 'noopener');
            return true;
          }
          return false;
        },
      },
      onUpdate: () => {
        if (silent) return;
        window.clearTimeout(timer);
        timer = window.setTimeout(() => {
          root.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('firma2:rich-text-change', { bubbles: true, detail: { html: editor.getHTML() } }));
        }, 300);
      },
      onTransaction: () => syncPressed(),
    });

    // ---- the toolbar ----
    const isActive: Record<string, () => boolean> = {
      bold: () => editor.isActive('bold'),
      italic: () => editor.isActive('italic'),
      'heading-2': () => editor.isActive('heading', { level: 2 }),
      'heading-3': () => editor.isActive('heading', { level: 3 }),
      'bullet-list': () => editor.isActive('bulletList'),
      'ordered-list': () => editor.isActive('orderedList'),
      blockquote: () => editor.isActive('blockquote'),
      link: () => editor.isActive('link'),
    };
    const run: Record<string, () => void> = {
      bold: () => editor.chain().focus().toggleBold().run(),
      italic: () => editor.chain().focus().toggleItalic().run(),
      'heading-2': () => editor.chain().focus().toggleHeading({ level: 2 }).run(),
      'heading-3': () => editor.chain().focus().toggleHeading({ level: 3 }).run(),
      'bullet-list': () => editor.chain().focus().toggleBulletList().run(),
      'ordered-list': () => editor.chain().focus().toggleOrderedList().run(),
      blockquote: () => editor.chain().focus().toggleBlockquote().run(),
      link: () => openLink(),
      image: () => pickImages(),
      alt: () => openAlt(),
      'remove-image': () => editor.chain().focus().deleteSelection().run(),
      file: () => pickFiles(),
      'remove-file': () => editor.chain().focus().deleteSelection().run(),
    };
    function syncPressed(): void {
      // The lego's WRAPPER is hidden, not the <button> the data-* lands on —
      // hiding only the button left empty wrappers holding gaps in the bar.
      const on = editor.isActive('image') ? 'image' : editor.isActive('fileEmbed') ? 'file' : 'text';
      toolbar.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-for]').forEach((b) => {
        (b.parentElement ?? b).style.display = b.dataset.for === on ? '' : 'none';
      });
      toolbar.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cmd][aria-pressed]').forEach((b) => {
        b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(isActive[b.dataset.cmd ?? '']?.() ?? false));
      });
    }
    // Tiptap repositions its menus on every scroll and, doing so, makes them
    // visible whether or not they were showing (updatePosition sets
    // visibility unconditionally). One editor on a page hid the bug; the
    // intake builder's several did not. A menu only stays up for the editor
    // you are in, or while you are using the menu itself.
    for (const bar of [toolbar, insertBar]) {
      new MutationObserver(() => {
        if (bar.style.visibility === 'visible' && !editor.view.hasFocus() && !bar.contains(document.activeElement)) bar.style.visibility = 'hidden';
      }).observe(bar, { attributeFilter: ['style'] });
    }
    for (const bar of [toolbar, insertBar]) {
      bar.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
        const cmd = (event.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLElement>('[data-cmd]')?.dataset.cmd;
        if (cmd) run[cmd]?.();
      });
    }

    // ---- images ----
    const imagesIn = (list: FileList | null | undefined): File[] =>
      Array.from(list ?? []).filter((f) => f.type.startsWith('image/'));
    const fail = (message: string) =>
      root.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('firma2:rich-text-error', { bubbles: true, detail: { message } }));
    // A plan's file storage is a limit like any other: what's stored stays; nothing more goes in.
    const storageFull = (): boolean => {
      if (!atLimit('storage')) return false;
      const plan = readPlan();
      fail(`${PLAN_NAME[plan]} includes ${limitOf('storage', plan)} GB of file storage, and it's full. Remove files or upgrade to add more.`);
      return true;
    };

    async function insertImages(files: File[], at?: number): Promise<void> {
      if (files.length && storageFull()) return;
      let pos = at;
      for (const file of files) {
        if (file.size > maxBytes) {
          fail(`${file.name} is over ${root.dataset.imageMaxMb} MB. Use a smaller image.`);
          continue;
        }
        const stored = root.firma2StoreImage ? await root.firma2StoreImage(file) : { src: URL.createObjectURL(file) };
        if (!stored) {
          fail(`${file.name} couldn’t be saved in this browser.`);
          continue;
        }
        // The file name, minus its extension, until someone writes better alt text.
        const node = { type: 'image', attrs: { src: stored.src, fileId: stored.fileId ?? null, alt: file.name.replace(/\.[^.]+$/, '') } };
        const chain = editor.chain().focus();
        (pos === undefined ? chain.insertContent(node) : chain.insertContentAt(pos, node)).run();
        pos = undefined;
      }
    }

    // ---- files ----
    async function insertFiles(files: File[], at?: number): Promise<void> {
      if (files.length && storageFull()) return;
      let pos = at;
      for (const file of files) {
        if (file.size > fileMaxBytes) {
          fail(`${file.name} is over ${root.dataset.fileMaxMb} MB. Use a smaller file.`);
          continue;
        }
        const stored = root.firma2StoreFile
          ? await root.firma2StoreFile(file)
          : { src: URL.createObjectURL(file), fileId: crypto.randomUUID() };
        if (!stored?.fileId) {
          fail(`${file.name} couldn’t be saved in this browser.`);
          continue;
        }
        placed.set(stored.fileId, stored.src);
        const node = { type: 'fileEmbed', attrs: { fileId: stored.fileId, name: file.name, type: file.type, size: file.size } };
        const chain = editor.chain().focus();
        (pos === undefined ? chain.insertContent(node) : chain.insertContentAt(pos, node)).run();
        pos = undefined;
      }
    }

    /** Images go in as images, everything else as files, in the order given. */
    async function insertDropped(list: FileList | globalThis.FileList, at?: number): Promise<void> {
      const all = Array.from(list as globalThis.FileList);
      const images = imagesIn(list as globalThis.FileList);
      await insertImages(images, at);
      await insertFiles(all.filter((f) => !images.includes(f)), images.length ? undefined : at);
    }

    // The OS file picker. A detached <input type="file"> is the only way to
    // open it; it is never rendered, so it is not a control on the page.
    function pick(accept: string, then: (files: globalThis.FileList | null) => void): void {
      const input = document.createElement('input');
      input.type = 'file';
      input.accept = accept;
      input.multiple = true;
      input.addEventListener('change', () => then(input.files));
      input.click();
    }
    function pickImages(): void {
      pick('image/*', (list) => void insertImages(imagesIn(list)));
    }
    function pickFiles(): void {
      pick('', (list) => void insertFiles(Array.from(list ?? [])));
    }

    function openAlt(): void {
      customElements.whenDefined('esa-dialog').then(() => {
        altField.value = (editor.getAttributes('image').alt as string | undefined) ?? '';
        altDialog.show();
        requestAnimationFrame(() => altField.focus());
      });
    }
    root.querySelector('[data-alt-save]')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      altDialog.close();
      editor.chain().focus().updateAttributes('image', { alt: (altField.value ?? '').trim() }).run();
    });
    root.querySelector('[data-alt-cancel]')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      altDialog.close();
      editor.commands.focus();
    });

    // ---- links ----
    function openLink(): void {
      customElements.whenDefined('esa-dialog').then(() => {
        urlField.value = (editor.getAttributes('link').href as string | undefined) ?? '';
        urlField.errorText = '';
        // style.display, not `hidden`: the button's own display rule outranks
        // the UA's [hidden], so the attribute alone leaves it on screen.
        const remove = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-link-remove]')!;
        (remove.parentElement ?? remove).style.display = editor.isActive('link') ? '' : 'none';
        dialog.show();
        requestAnimationFrame(() => urlField.focus());
      });
    }
    const saveLink = (): void => {
      const raw = (urlField.value ?? '').trim();
      if (!raw) {
        urlField.errorText = 'Enter a web address.';
        urlField.focus();
        return;
      }
      const href = /^[a-z][a-z0-9+.-]*:/i.test(raw) ? raw : `https://${raw}`;
      dialog.close();
      editor.chain().focus().extendMarkRange('link').setLink({ href }).run();
    };
    root.querySelector('[data-link-save]')?.addEventListener('click', saveLink);
    urlField.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
      if ((event as KeyboardEvent).key === 'Enter') saveLink();
    });
    root.querySelector('[data-link-remove]')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      dialog.close();
      editor.chain().focus().extendMarkRange('link').unsetLink().run();
    });
    root.querySelector('[data-link-cancel]')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      dialog.close();
      editor.commands.focus();
    });
    // Mod+K opens the same dialog, the shortcut every editor uses for links.
    mount.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
      if ((event.metaKey || event.ctrlKey) && event.key.toLowerCase() === 'k') {
        event.preventDefault();
        openLink();
      }
    });

    // ---- block actions: the grip's menu and the canvas keys ----
    // Each keeps the caret where it was inside the block it moved or copied.
    function blockAction(action: string, pos: number): boolean {
      const { state } = editor;
      const node = state.doc.nodeAt(pos);
      if (!node) return false;
      const index = state.doc.resolve(pos).index(0);
      const end = pos + node.nodeSize;
      const offset = Math.max(0, Math.min(state.selection.from - pos, node.nodeSize - 1));
      const caretAt = (tr: typeof state.tr, at: number) => tr.setSelection(TextSelection.near(tr.doc.resolve(Math.min(at + Math.max(offset, 1), tr.doc.content.size))));
      if (action === 'duplicate') {
        editor.view.dispatch(caretAt(state.tr.insert(end, node.copy(node.content)), end).scrollIntoView());
      } else if (action === 'up') {
        if (index === 0) return true;
        const prevPos = pos - state.doc.child(index - 1).nodeSize;
        editor.view.dispatch(caretAt(state.tr.delete(pos, end).insert(prevPos, node), prevPos).scrollIntoView());
      } else if (action === 'down') {
        if (index >= state.doc.childCount - 1) return true;
        const next = state.doc.child(index + 1);
        const tr = state.tr.insert(end + next.nodeSize, node).delete(pos, end);
        editor.view.dispatch(caretAt(tr, pos + next.nodeSize).scrollIntoView());
      } else if (action === 'delete') {
        editor.view.dispatch(state.tr.delete(pos, end));
      } else if (action.startsWith('into:')) {
        const kind = action.slice(5);
        const chain = editor.chain().focus().command(({ tr }) => {
          tr.setSelection(TextSelection.near(tr.doc.resolve(pos + 1)));
          return true;
        }).clearNodes();
        if (kind === 'heading-2' || kind === 'heading-3') chain.setHeading({ level: kind === 'heading-2' ? 2 : 3 });
        if (kind === 'bullet-list') chain.toggleBulletList();
        if (kind === 'ordered-list') chain.toggleOrderedList();
        if (kind === 'blockquote') chain.toggleBlockquote();
        chain.run();
      } else return false;
      editor.commands.focus();
      return true;
    }

    if (canvas && slash) {
      slash.addEventListener('insert-choose', (event) => {
        const id = (event as CustomEvent<{ id: string }>).detail.id;
        if (slashRange) editor.chain().focus().deleteRange(slashRange).run();
        slashRange = null;
        run[id]?.();
      });
    }

    // THE GRIP follows the pointer from block to block, in the margin beside
    // the block's first line. It keeps the block it was opened on while its
    // menu is up, so moving the pointer to a menu item never retargets it.
    if (canvas && grip) {
      const view = editor.view;
      let target: { pos: number; dom: HTMLElement } | null = null;
      const topBlock = (el: EventTarget | null): HTMLElement | null => {
        let node = el instanceof HTMLElement ? el : null;
        while (node && node.parentElement !== view.dom) node = node.parentElement;
        return node;
      };
      const posOf = (dom: HTMLElement): number | null => {
        let found: number | null = null;
        view.state.doc.forEach((_n, offset) => {
          if (found == null && view.nodeDOM(offset) === dom) found = offset;
        });
        return found;
      };
      const itemsFor = (pos: number) => {
        const node = view.state.doc.nodeAt(pos)!;
        const index = view.state.doc.resolve(pos).index(0);
        const kind = kindOf(node);
        const items: Menu['items'] = [
          { label: 'Duplicate', action: 'duplicate' },
          { label: 'Move up', action: 'up', disabled: index === 0 },
          { label: 'Move down', action: 'down', disabled: index === view.state.doc.childCount - 1 },
        ];
        if (kind) {
          items.push({ label: '', divider: true });
          KINDS.filter((k) => k.id !== kind).forEach((k) => items.push({ label: `Turn into ${k.label}`, action: `into:${k.id}` }));
        }
        items.push({ label: '', divider: true }, { label: 'Delete', action: 'delete', variant: 'danger' });
        return items;
      };
      const place = (dom: HTMLElement) => {
        const pos = posOf(dom);
        if (pos == null) return;
        target = { pos, dom };
        const r = dom.getBoundingClientRect();
        const host = root.getBoundingClientRect();
        const line = Math.min(r.height, parseFloat(getComputedStyle(dom).lineHeight) || 24);
        grip.style.top = `${r.top - host.top + (line - 40) / 2}px`;
        grip.hidden = false;
        customElements.whenDefined('esa-dropdown-menu').then(() => (grip.items = itemsFor(pos)));
      };
      mount.addEventListener('mousemove', (event) => {
        if (!editor.isEditable || grip.open) return;
        const dom = topBlock(event.target);
        if (dom && dom !== target?.dom) place(dom);
      });
      root.addEventListener('mouseleave', () => {
        if (!grip.open) grip.hidden = true;
      });
      grip.addEventListener('menu-action', (event) => {
        if (!target) return;
        blockAction((event as CustomEvent<string>).detail, target.pos);
        grip.hidden = true;
        target = null;
      });
      // Dragged, the grip carries its block: ProseMirror moves a dragged
      // node selection on drop, as it does an image.
      grip.addEventListener('dragstart', (event) => {
        if (!target || !event.dataTransfer) return;
        const selection = NodeSelection.create(view.state.doc, target.pos);
        view.dispatch(view.state.tr.setSelection(selection));
        (view as unknown as { dragging: unknown }).dragging = { slice: selection.content(), move: true };
        event.dataTransfer.clearData();
        event.dataTransfer.setData('text/html', target.dom.outerHTML);
        event.dataTransfer.effectAllowed = 'move';
        event.dataTransfer.setDragImage(target.dom, 0, 0);
      });
      grip.addEventListener('dragend', () => {
        grip.hidden = true;
        target = null;
      });
      // A change elsewhere may have moved the block under the grip.
      editor.on('update', () => {
        if (!grip.open) {
          grip.hidden = true;
          target = null;
        }
      });
    }

    // ---- content in ----
    root.addEventListener('firma2:rich-text-set', (event) => {
      const html = (event as CustomEvent<{ html: string }>).detail?.html ?? '';
      silent = true;
      editor.commands.setContent(html, { emitUpdate: false });
      silent = false;
    });
    root.addEventListener('firma2:rich-text-editable', (event) => {
      const editable = Boolean((event as CustomEvent<{ editable: boolean }>).detail?.editable);
      editor.setEditable(editable, false);
      root.toggleAttribute('data-readonly', !editable);
    });
    root.addEventListener('firma2:rich-text-focus', () => {
      editor.commands.focus('end');
    });
  };

  document.querySelectorAll<Root>('[data-rich-text]').forEach(mountRichText);
  // An editor added after load — cloned from a template, as the intake
  // builder's text blocks are — asks to be mounted with this event.
  document.addEventListener('firma2:rich-text-mount', (event) => mountRichText(event.target as Root));
</script>

<style>
  /* Tiptap moves the toolbar to <body>, so its rules key on its own class
     (which keeps Astro's scope attribute). esa-popover's surface, token for token. */
  .firma2-rich-text__toolbar {
    visibility: hidden;
    /* Out of the flow until Tiptap first moves it to <body> and positions it,
       so an editor that has not shown it yet is as tall as its text. */
    position: absolute;
    /* Its own width before it is first measured. Tiptap sets max-content only
       AFTER positioning, so the first placement measured a full-width flex row
       and centred it off the left edge of the screen. */
    width: max-content;
    z-index: var(--z-popover, 1000);
    padding: var(--spacing-100, 4px);
    background: var(--color-background-elevation-raised, #fcfcfc);
    border: var(--border-width-default, 1px) solid var(--color-border-default, #cecece);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.5rem);
    box-shadow: var(--elevation-4, 0 6px 24px -6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.07));
  }
  /* The pressed tool reads as selected — the lego's own hover fill, held. */
  .firma2-rich-text__toolbar :global([data-cmd][aria-pressed='true']) {
    background: var(--color-background-elevation-sunken, #f0f0f0);
    color: var(--color-content-brand, #2a7e3b);
  }

  /* As a canvas, the grip hangs in the margin left of the text, beside the
     block under the pointer; reading, there is none. */
  .firma2-rich-text[data-canvas] {
    position: relative;
  }
  .firma2-rich-text__grip {
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline-start: calc(-1 * (var(--control-height-md, 2.5rem) + var(--spacing-200, 0.5rem)));
    z-index: 1;
    /* The lego's own hook: room for "Turn into numbered list" on one line. */
    --dropdown-menu-min-width: 14rem;
  }
  .firma2-rich-text__grip[hidden],
  .firma2-rich-text[data-readonly] .firma2-rich-text__grip {
    display: none;
  }
  .firma2-rich-text__grip :global(button) {
    cursor: grab;
  }

  .firma2-rich-text :global(.firma2-rich-text__content) {
    min-block-size: 6rem;
    outline: none;
    color: var(--color-content-default, #202020);
  }
  /* Reading, the text is as tall as the text — the writing room above is
     for an empty editor you are about to type into. */
  .firma2-rich-text[data-readonly] :global(.firma2-rich-text__content) {
    min-block-size: 0;
  }
  /* Blocks space by role: a heading pulls away from what came before and sits
     close on what it names; paragraphs and lists take one body step. */
  .firma2-rich-text :global(.firma2-rich-text__content > * + *) {
    margin-block-start: var(--spacing-300, 0.75rem);
  }
  .firma2-rich-text :global(.firma2-rich-text__content > :is(h2, h3)) {
    margin-block-start: var(--spacing-600, 1.5rem);
  }
  .firma2-rich-text :global(.firma2-rich-text__content > :first-child) {
    margin-block-start: 0;
  }
  .firma2-rich-text :global(.firma2-rich-text__content :is(h2, h3, p)) {
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }
  .firma2-rich-text :global(.firma2-rich-text__content :is(ul, ol)) {
    margin: 0;
    padding-inline-start: var(--spacing-600, 1.5rem);
  }
  .firma2-rich-text :global(.firma2-rich-text__content li + li) {
    margin-block-start: var(--spacing-100, 4px);
  }
  .firma2-rich-text :global(.firma2-rich-text__content li p) {
    margin: 0;
  }
  /* A neutral rule, not a status colour: the quote is set apart, not flagged. */
  .firma2-rich-text :global(.firma2-rich-text__content blockquote) {
    margin-inline: 0;
    padding-inline-start: var(--spacing-400, 1rem);
    border-inline-start: 2px solid var(--color-border-default, #cecece);
    color: var(--color-content-default-secondary, #646464);
  }
  .firma2-rich-text :global(.firma2-rich-text__content a) {
    color: var(--color-content-brand, #2a7e3b);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  /* Images take the column's width at most, and show their selection with
     the focus ring's colour so a selected image reads as the thing the
     toolbar above it acts on. */
  .firma2-rich-text :global(.firma2-rich-text__image) {
    display: block;
    max-inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.5rem);
  }
  /* A file in the text: the PDF preview (when it is one) over its
     name-and-download row. The preview takes the column's width and about a
     page's first half — enough to know the document, short enough that the
     text keeps going; Full screen and Open in new tab are for the rest.
     Framed like the document view's. */
  .firma2-rich-text :global(.firma2-rich-text__file-frame) {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: min(60dvh, 30rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-default-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.5rem);
    background: var(--color-background-elevation-sunken);
  }
  /* The name row takes what the two buttons leave. */
  .firma2-rich-text :global(.firma2-rich-text__file-bar > esa-file-list) {
    flex: 1;
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }
  .firma2-rich-text :global(.firma2-rich-text__file.ProseMirror-selectednode) {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-border-focus, #2a7e3b);
    outline-offset: 2px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.5rem);
  }
  .firma2-rich-text :global(.firma2-rich-text__image.ProseMirror-selectednode) {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-border-focus, #2a7e3b);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  /* The placeholder, in unset ink, on the empty first line only. */
  .firma2-rich-text :global(.firma2-rich-text__content .is-editor-empty:first-child::before) {
    content: attr(data-placeholder);
    float: inline-start;
    block-size: 0;
    color: var(--color-content-default-secondary, #646464);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
</style>
